  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:07:44.389Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:07:44.374Z",
  "id": 203980134472578,
  "uuid": "fcdbfd37-8d20-48eb-9d28-78ddf76f6f0a",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "5380435e-177a-dbc2-929b-abf876d453d2",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "28b0bad9-ffcf-d3c0-fb9f-dc225279a80b",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This was part of discussions at the ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Covering Covid-19 webinar",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " hosted by AKU's Graduate School of Media and Communications (GSMC). The webinar looked at the role of images and satire in reporting on the pandemic, challenges facing the media and the future of journalism.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": " \"It is not about showing the images of the dead or stigmatizing the sick. It is about being creative in the angles that the media teases out daily. Personalizing the coverage will make it more impactful,\" said Joe Odindo, a communications consultant and panelist at the webinar.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The panelists, who consisted of GSMC alumni and media practitioners, noted that the pandemic has hastened a transition in the media industry that was long overdue. One of the recommendations was for the media to create value by selling content and diversifying on digital platforms in order to cater to a new generation of consumers.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "John Ngirachu, Senior Writer at Oxygène MCL, acknowledged that there has been a lack of creativity in the coverage of the pandemic, which he largely blamed on the lack of access to information on the pandemic. \"Media coverage has been hampered by the government's bureaucratic tendencies to democratize access to information, a responsibility that has previously been handled by the media.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This is the second webinar hosted by the Graduate School of Media and Communications that aims to address the challenges and opportunities in the media and communications sector. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "GSMC continues to invest in the improvement of the quality of media practitioners through its programs, some of which are designed specifically for the media fraternity. It is committed to keeping the knowledge discourse alive among media practitioners, and in so doing hopes to help contribute to quality training and nurturing of seasoned media practitioners.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Watch the full webinar below:",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "https://youtu.be/vXpP_IrI7Y0",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://youtu.be/vXpP_IrI7Y0",
